items.detail:
Add #register directly below the two charts on corrections.html: one row per finding, 33 in total, built from dashboard/corrections.json rounds[].findings[].

Columns:
- ID (C16.1 …);
- round;
- flaw (title);
- status (fixed / quantified);
- portfolio P&L effect where the C22/C23 bridge CSV quantifies it, else '—';
- tests pinning it (count). A count of 0 shows a 'gap' chip; currently 1 finding, C16 F4.
- link to the finding's anchor.

Add filter chips All / Quantified / No test as buttons with aria-pressed, implemented in desk.js. Without JS every row is visible.

Postmortem rounds become <details>, open for the newest round (C23) only. The register is never collapsed.

Verified: 8 rounds with 5, 4, 1, 1, 1, 3, 7 and 11 findings (33 total): 30 fixed, 3 quantified, 1 without tests.

New pure module dashboard/desk_surface.py (no Flask). It provides:
- svi_w(k, slice) and svi_atm_skew(slice);
- delta_strike(slice, target): brentq on the undiscounted forward Black call delta N(−k/√w + √w/2) over the certificate range k ∈ [−3, 2];
- delta_grid(surface_json, residuals, vix_rep);
- constant_maturity(grid, days = (30, 61, 91, 182, 365)): linear in total variance at fixed delta between bracketing listed expiries; never extrapolated, so '—' outside the listed T range.

Inputs per session:
- surface.json surfaces.svi_cal.params.slices[] (a, b, rho, m, sigma, T, expiry);
- term_structure[] (forward, atm_vol_svi_cal, n_quotes, median_half_spread_vp);
- vix_replication.json strip[] (var_swap_vol, vs_minus_atm_vp);
- residuals.parquet svi_cal rows (min/max k per expiry, for the extrapolation test).

New Surface panel #delta-grid, first on the page, with a tabs toggle 'Listed expiries (17) | Constant maturity (5)'. Columns:
- Expiry, T (d), F;
- 10ΔP, 25ΔP, ATMF, 25ΔC, 10ΔC;
- RR25, BF25, RR10, BF10 (RR = σC − σP, BF = (σC + σP)/2 − σATMF);
- ATM skew in vol pts per 0.1 ln-moneyness;
- VS vol, VS − ATMF;
- median half-spread (vol pts), quotes.

Cell styling:
- Vol cells use the CIVIDIS_11 tint; RR/BF use the diverging ramp.
- A pillar whose k lies outside that expiry's quoted k range is shown with '◇ extrapolated'. It is excluded from RR/BF, which show '—'.

Caption: 'undiscounted forward delta on the slice's own vol (not premium-adjusted); ATMF = ln(K/F) = 0; RR = call − put (negative = puts over calls); values of the fitted SVI-cal surface, not raw quotes'.

'Surface state' KPI row above the existing error tiles: 1M ATMF, 1M RR25, 1M BF25, 1M VS − ATMF, ATMF slope 1M → 1Y.

Overview #state-fit gains one line: '1M ATMF 13.8 · RR25 −5.8 · BF25 +0.8 (surface 2026-10-16, 5 sessions old)'.

At < 600 px the grid is a labelled focusable scroll region (role=region, aria-label, tabindex=0) inside its panel; the page itself never overflows.

Verified on 2026-10-16:
- 2026-11-16 (31 d): ATMF 13.82, RR25 −5.82, BF25 +0.84, RR10 −13.91, BF10 +3.89.
- 2027-04-16 (182 d): ATMF 15.27, RR25 −6.36, BF25 +0.88.
- 25ΔP k = −0.033 and 10ΔP k = −0.090 at 31 d.

Row order: BREACH, then WATCH, then OK, then INFO; within a status, by model. Today the 13 checks are sorted by model ID.

Summary strip '6 breach · 3 watch · 3 OK · 1 info' (counts from the RAG tally). Each chip is a filter button with aria-pressed. Without JS all rows show.

For each numeric check, a server-rendered SVG bullet of about 120×10 px:
- OK band [0, g], watch (g, a], breach up to max(1.5a, value), and a tick at the value;
- role=img with an aria-label such as 'value 2.96; OK ≤ 1.5, watch ≤ 3';
- limits from MONITOR_LIMITS (app.py:4059).

History cell:
- One dot per stored session (oldest → newest, dated in the title), coloured by today's limits, plus min–max and 'rank today: worst of 5'.
- Each history value comes from the same function that computes today's value, applied per session to:
  - the gated joint_cal pickles (OOS, worst short-dated expiry, VIX RMSE, parameters on bound);
  - scorecard.json (Heston OOS median |z|);
  - surface/index.json (executable-arbitrage share);
  - vix_replication.json (replication gap);
  - the β-chain computation (ATM/VIX).
- Checks with no history say 'single observation'.
- Label: 'stored sessions, irregular spacing; today's limits applied retroactively'. Dots, not a line; never 'control limits'.

Links:
- Rows get id='check-<slug>'.
- Each value cell links to its evidence panel, e.g. calibration.html#oos, #identifiability, #vixleg; surface.html#arbitrage, #vix-replication, #scorecard; research.html#beta-chains, #research-classifier.
- Each evidence panel shows a chip 'Monitored · <model> · <status>' linking back to model-risk.html#check-<slug>.

Replace each unlabelled sparkline on the Calibration parameter tiles with a server-rendered SVG dot plot:
- one dot per gated session, value ± 2·SE (diagnostics/<s>.json identifiability.standard_errors);
- box bounds (sigma_profile.production_box) as dashed lines, with min/max tick labels;
- a parameter in identifiability.on_bound (σ) sits on the dashed line with no whisker.

Label: 'Gauss–Newton curvature scale, not a confidence interval'.

Tile sub-lines:
- θ: '√θ = 22.35% long-run vol';
- v0: '√v₀ = 18.54% spot vol';
- κ: 'half-life 35.0 sessions (ln2/κ × 252)'.
All three verified for 2026-10-16.

Today the Surface #chart-slices tooltip is an item tooltip: '−0.129 / 2026-11-16 mid 29.21' (verified). It has no strike, no bid/ask and no model values, it leaks a raw series name, and it shows nothing off-marker. The Calibration smiles behave the same way.

Spec additions (server, app.py smile builders):
- per expiry: forward F (term_structure.forward), T, and the strike grid step;
- per quote: right, in_sample, arb_exec and repair flag;
- client-derived values: strike = round-to-grid(F·e^k), forward delta N(d1) from mid IV, and z = (model − mid)/half-spread. Model IVs at the quotes' x are already in the spec (test_smile_slice_model_points_share_the_quotes_x_values), so these cost no bytes.

desk.js:
(1) Axis-trigger tooltip with a custom nearest-quote lookup by x-pixel distance within the visible group:
- header 'K 7,560 P · ln(K/F) −0.014 · Δ −0.42 · 31 d';
- rows: bid / mid / ask IV, then each visible model's IV and z with an inside/outside glyph, then flags 'fit anchor', 'in executable arb row', 'repaired';
- footnote 'Yahoo close, no quote time';
- series names have the 'YYYY-MM-DD ' prefix stripped.

(2) A second grid of about 70 px under the smile sharing the x axis:
- z per quote for the visible models (Calibration: Heston only, anchors marked);
- ±1 band shaded and labelled 'inside the spread', ±2 dashed;
- y clipped at ±10 with a clip marker.

(3) Segmented control 'ln(K/F) | forward Δ' (buttons, aria-pressed):
- Δ mode plots OTM forward delta (puts left, calls right) with gridlines at 10/25/50Δ;
- the selected expiry is kept.

Keyboard path: a focusable readout line under the chart (same pattern as the heatmap readout). Arrow keys step through quotes and show the same text, because canvas tooltips are not keyboard reachable.

Server:
- data-exp on each row of the IV heatmap, the residual heatmap and the P2.1 delta grid;
- a <button> inside each th[scope=row].

desk.js — selecting an expiry happens on:
- click or Enter on a row header;
- a click on a #chart-by-expiry category;
- the global keys '[' and ']' (previous/next; added to the shortcut dialog).

The selection then:
- runs the existing smile tab select();
- writes exp= into the hash;
- sets aria-current='true' on the matching rows in all three tables;
- draws an x markLine on #chart-by-expiry;
- names the expiry in the heat readout;
- scrolls the smile into view only if it is offscreen.

The no-JS view is unchanged.

Add one desk.js mechanism: data-chart-group='<name>' on chart elements. It provides:
- echarts.connect(group), which ships in echarts/core, for a linked axisPointer and tooltip;
- a shared inside dataZoom, with zoom presets that drive the group;
- an optional shared legend bar (data-legend-for lists every member).

Research:
- Move #drawdown and #rolling (today s6 + s6, h180, on different extents) under #equity, all s12 with the same grid.left/right, so the plot areas align.
- Group the three with the slider on #equity only; the 1Y/3Y/All presets drive the group.
- Draw the R2 shading on all three.
- Clicking a #chart-annual bar zooms the group to that calendar year.

Calibration, the six #smile-* panels:
- one shared ln(K/F) domain (min/max over the six, computed server-side from the data, so nothing clips) and a common y tick step;
- one legend bar above the grid driving all six;
- connect for a linked axisPointer;
- a compact per-panel header: expiry, days, Heston inside-spread % and median |z|;
- one group-level Table/CSV with an expiry column, replacing the six pairs.

items.acceptance:
1) A pytest over every frozen page's JSON specs checks:
   (a) model-keyed series have colour == model_colour(key) and label == model_label(key);
   (b) no non-model series on a model page uses a model colour;
   (c) tenor series use the ramp, monotone in T;
   (d) no series on y = P&L/return charts is within ΔE76 < 25 of the pos/neg fills;
   (e) market and Cboe series use 'headline';
   (f) no series uses 'info'.
   This extends test_one_colour_per_model_on_every_surface_chart.
2) Heat test: only P&L heatmaps use PNL_DIV; every .ramp has two numeric endpoints; Playwright finds no visible text < 10.5 px in table.heat.
3) Tooltips on #chart-ts, #chart-oos and #chart-strip show 'VIX3M', '93 d', 'vol pts' and '%' respectively.
4) Series still reach 3:1 against the panels (existing contrast test); axe reports 0 violations.
